I call the salon again.
The receptionist answers the phone.
"Hello, I am Maya," I say.
"I have an appointment on Saturday."
"It is at eleven o'clock in the morning."
"But I have some work at eleven o'clock."
"Is the afternoon time free?" I ask.
The receptionist checks the calendar.
"Yes, the afternoon time is free," she says.
"What time do you want to come?"
"Is half past two in the afternoon fine?" I ask.
"Yes, half past two is fine," the receptionist replies.
"So now your appointment is on Saturday at half past two."
"Thank you very much," I say.
I hang up the phone.
Now my morning is free.
I always keep my calendar organized.
Now I can meet Asha at eleven o'clock.
